     "text": "{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Two blocks are not enough. h3_0 (AND) can only be cut by blocking one of h3_0, h1_0, h2_0 or h1_1. h3_2 needs h3_2 itself blocked, or both h1_2 and h2_2 blocked; h2_2 cannot be cut upstream because it has edge1 as a direct parent. h3_1 needs h3_1 itself blocked, or h1_2, h2_2 and h2_1 all blocked. With only two blocks, one must go to the h3_0 branch, and none of its options also cuts h3_2 or h3_1. The single remaining block cannot cut both h3_2 and h3_1. Blocking h3_0, h3_1 and h3_2 makes crown:obtain unreachable, so the minimum is 3.\"}"
    }
